-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Martianoids
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Martianoids (1987)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         5df07fbd5dabdcb9a909b86cf690a4e8

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Your robot in blue with a white dome, the Martianoids in purple,
              the pylons cyan-striped on orange bases, items in their own
              colours and explosions orange, on a dark blue checker floor; the
              panel, score, battery and map unchanged. No outlines added. A
              painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original (-1.37% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe 9967
              (the player's own update); 3 trials per scene, each at its own R
              and raster phase, 240 updates; every window and every single
              update faster than the original, none slower; player state equal
              to the original at every update)

  Changes     1.0: Enhanced colours, painted by Jon Attree, drawn in order on
              a double-buffered Layer 2 view inside the original play area;
              the original loading screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); the game's speed restored after every
              hook; three cheats from the archive, corrected.

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keyboard, 2 Kempston, 3 cursor or 4
              Interface II, then 0 to start. The default is the original game,
              picture and all: its play area is drawn in one colour, so it
              never had colour clash; the patch gives it Sinclair's whole 48K
              ROM so it runs on NextZXOS 26.11. Enhanced paints the figures in
              their own colours and lays a coloured checker floor, drawn on
              the Next's Layer 2 behind the original's own screen, so the
              game's masks, XOR effects, panel and map stay as they were. The
              original 48K game with its beeper sound; fits a 1MB Next. Known
              issues: the original's low update rate and its small frame-to-
              frame timing variation remain; in JNext it runs 1.2 to 1.4
              percent faster than the original in every scene measured.
              Missing: not reached in testing: natural play to the end,
              joysticks; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite battery
   3  Protect sectors

  The archive's POKEs checked against this exact release. Infinite lives
  covers both of the original's loss paths (the archive missed one); Infinite
  battery covers the meter and both collision drains; Protect sectors takes
  the original's own protected-sector branch instead of the archive's unsafe
  RET.

